# U-C2 settings.json patch (pre-staged)

**Why pre-staged:** at the time U-C2 shipped (2026-05-10), peer chat
DESKTOP--25664 had an active claim on `C:/Users/wompu/.claude/settings.json`.
Per lane-discipline doctrine I did not edit settings.json directly. The hook
file is committed and the bundle daemon is running; just needs this 5-line
registration to wire in.

## Apply when settings.json is no longer claimed

In `C:/Users/wompu/.claude/settings.json`, find the **UserPromptSubmit**
hooks block. Insert this entry as the FIRST hook (so the bundle injection
arrives before any of the legacy 24 individual injectors):

```diff
     "UserPromptSubmit": [
       {
         "matcher": "",
         "hooks": [
+          {
+            "type": "command",
+            "command": "\"H:/.claude/bin/portable-node\" H:/prism/.claude/hooks/prompt-context-inject.mjs",
+            "timeout": 1500
+          },
           {
             "type": "command",
             "command": "\"H:/.claude/bin/portable-node\" H:/prism/.claude/hooks/ollama-auto-router.mjs",
             "timeout": 5000
           },
```

After the edit:
1. Validate JSON: `node -e "JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('C:/Users/wompu/.claude/settings.json'))"`
2. Verify mirror sync (c-to-h-mirror PostToolUse hook should fire on the Edit; if not, manually `cp C:/Users/wompu/.claude/settings.json H:/.claude/settings.json`).
3. Confirm the bundle daemon is alive: `node H:/prism/scripts/daemon-supervisor.mjs status context-bundle`. If not, restart it:
   `node H:/prism/scripts/daemon-supervisor.mjs start context-bundle -- "H:/Tools/nodejs/node.exe" "H:/prism/.claude/helpers/prism-awareness-bundle.mjs" --daemon --tick=30`

## What the hook does

`H:/prism/.claude/hooks/prompt-context-inject.mjs`:

- Fires on every UserPromptSubmit
- Reads `state/shared/context-bundle.json` (single fs read, ~200ms typical)
- Filters bundle body slice by prompt keywords (one regex pass)
- Emits ONE compact `additionalContext` block (≤2KB) with:
  - PRISM context header (bundle age, byte size)
  - Top relevant section based on prompt keywords
  - Pointer to full bundle files
- Fail-open: missing/stale/unreadable bundle → silent `{continue:true}`, legacy 24 injectors carry on

## Roll-out (per spec)

This is **Phase 1**: hook is added ALONGSIDE the 24 legacy injectors. Both run.
Once we confirm the bundle output covers their content, **Phase 2 (U-C4)** retires
the 24 individuals. That's a separate spec unit.

## Rollback

`PRISM_PROMPT_CONTEXT_INJECT_OFF=1` in env disables the hook.

